<style>
  @page { size: A4; margin: 0; }
  .page {
    width: 794px; height: 1123px;
    padding: 50px 60px; box-sizing: border-box;
    overflow: hidden; page-break-after: always;
    position: relative;
    font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Helvetica", Arial, "DejaVu Sans", "Liberation Sans";
  }
  .page:last-child { page-break-after: auto; }
  table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }
  td {
    padding: 4px 0;
    vertical-align: top;
  }
  .header-row td {
    font-weight: bold;
  }
  .form-title {
    font-size: 24pt;
    font-weight: bold;
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  .section-header {
    font-weight: bold;
    margin-top: 15px;
    margin-bottom: 5px;
  }
  .signature-line {
    margin-top: 50px;
  }
</style>

<div class="page">
  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start;">
    <div>
      <div style="font-size: 10pt; margin-bottom: 5px;">
        <span data-field="payer_name_line1">{{ payer_name_line1 }}</span>
      </div>
      <div style="display: flex; gap: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
        <div style="display: flex; align-items: center;">
          <input type="checkbox" style="margin-right: 5px;">
          <span data-field="void_indicator">{{ void_indicator }}</span>
        </div>
        <div style="display: flex; align-items: center;">
          <input type="checkbox" style="margin-right: 5px;">
          <span data-field="corrected_indicator">{{ corrected_indicator }}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div style="text-align: right;">
      <div style="font-size: 10pt;">OMB No. 1545-0238</div>
      <div style="font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold;">2013</div>
      <div style="font-size: 16pt; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 5px;">Form W-2G</div>
      <div style="font-size: 12pt; margin-top: 10px;">Certain Gambling Winnings</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <table style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <thead>
      <tr class="header-row">
        <td style="width: 10%;">3 Type of wager</td>
        <td style="width: 10%;">4 Federal income tax withheld</td>
        <td style="width: 10%;">5 Transaction</td>
        <td style="width: 10%;">6 Race</td>
        <td style="width: 10%;">7 Winnings from identical wagers</td>
        <td style="width: 10%;">8 Cashier</td>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><span data-field="wager_type">{{ wager_type }}</span></td>
        <td>$ <span data-field="federal_tax_withheld">{{ federal_tax_withheld }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="transaction_id">{{ transaction_id }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="race_id">{{ race_id }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="identical_wager_amount">{{ identical_wager_amount }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="cashier_id">{{ cashier_id }}</span></td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <table style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <tr>
      <td style="width: 30%;">Federal identification number</td>
      <td style="width: 30%;">Telephone number</td>
      <td style="width: 30%;">9 Winner's taxpayer identification no.</td>
      <td style="width: 10%;">10 Window</td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between;">
      <div style="width: 45%;">
        <div style="font-weight: bold;">WINNER'S name</div>
        <div style="margin-top: 5px;"><span data-field="winner_name">{{ winner_name }}</span></div>
      </div>
      <div style="width: 45%; text-align: right;">
        <div style="font-weight: bold;">11 First I.D.</div>
        <div style="margin-top: 5px;"><span data-field="first_id">{{ first_id }}</span></div>
        <div style="font-weight: bold;">12 Second I.D.</div>
        <div style="margin-top: 5px;"><span data-field="second_id">{{ second_id }}</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <table style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <tr>
      <td style="width: 50%;">Street address (including apt. no.)</td>
      <td style="width: 50%;">13 State/Payer's state identification no.</td>
      <td style="width: 20%;">14 State winnings</td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  <table style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <tr>
      <td style="width: 33%;">City or town, province or state, country, and ZIP or foreign postal code</td>
      <td style="width: 33%;">15 State income tax withheld</td>
      <td style="width: 33%;">16 Local winnings</td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  <table style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <tr>
      <td style="width: 33%;"></td>
      <td style="width: 33%;">17 Local income tax withheld</td>
      <td style="width: 33%;">18 Name of locality</td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
    <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Under penalties of perjury, I declare that, to the best of my knowledge and belief, the name, address, and taxpayer identification number that I have furnished correctly identify me as the recipient of this payment and any payments from identical wagers, and that no other person is entitled to any part of these payments.</p>
  </div>

  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-top: 50px;">
    <div style="width: 30%;">
      <div style="font-weight: bold;">Signature</div>
      <div style="margin-top: 5px;"><span data-field="signature_date">{{ signature_date }}</span></div>
      <div style="margin-top: 5px;">Form W-2G</div>
    </div>
    <div style="width: 30%; text-align: right;">
      <div style="font-weight: bold;">Date</div>
      <div style="margin-top: 5px;"><span data-field="date_signed">{{ date_signed }}</span></div>
      <div style="margin-top: 5px;">www.irs.gov/w2g</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="margin-top: 50px; font-size: 9pt; text-align: center;">
    <p>Do Not Cut or Separate Forms on This Page — Do Not Cut or Separate Forms on This Page</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div style="font-size: 10pt; margin-bottom: 15px;">
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between;">
      <div style="width: 50%;">
        <div style="font-weight: bold;">Instructions to Winner</div>
        <div style="margin-top: 10px;">
          <p>Box 1. The payer must furnish a Form W-2G to you if you receive:</p>
          <ul style="padding-left: 20px; margin-top: 5px;">
            <li>$1,000 or more in gambling winnings from bingo or slot machines.</li>
            <li>$1,500 or more in proceeds (the amount of winnings minus the amount of the wager) from:</li>
            <li>More than $5,000 in winnings (reduced by the wager or bonus) from a poker tournament.</li>
            <li>$600 or more in gambling winnings (except winnings from bingo, slot machines, and poker tournaments) and the payout is at least 300 times the amount of the wager; or</li>
            <li>Any other gambling winnings subject to federal income tax.</li>
          </ul>
          <p style="margin-top: 10px;">Generally, report all gambling winnings on the "Other income" line of Form 1040. You can deduct gambling losses and deductions, but you cannot deduct losses that exceed your winnings. Keep an accurate record of your winnings and losses, and be able to prove those amounts with receipts, tickets, statements, or similar items that you have saved. For more information, see Pub. 529, Taxable and Nontaxable Income.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div style="width: 50%;">
        <div style="font-weight: bold;">Box 4. Any federal income tax withheld on these winnings is shown in this box. Federal income tax must be withheld on certain winnings.</div>
        <div style="margin-top: 10px;">
          <p>Certain winnings that are not subject to regular gambling withholding may be subject to backup withholding if you did not provide your federal identification number to the payer. If you did not provide your federal identification number to the payer, the payer may withhold 24% of the winnings as federal income tax. See Pub. 505, Tax Withholding and Estimated Tax, for additional information.</p>
          <p style="margin-top: 10px;">Signature. You must sign Form W-2G if you are the only person to whom the winnings are payable. If the winnings are payable to multiple persons, you must sign the return signed to the payer, who will give you your copies.</p>
          <p style="margin-top: 10px;">Other winners. Prepare Form 5754, Statement by Person(s) Receiving Gambling Winnings, in the 2013 Instructions for Form W-2G and 5754.</p>
          <p style="margin-top: 10px;">Future developments. Information about any future changes to this form will be posted at www.irs.gov/w2g.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div style="font-size: 10pt; margin-bottom: 15px;">
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between;">
      <div style="width: 50%;">
        <div style="font-weight: bold;">Instructions to Complete Form W-2G</div>
        <div style="margin-top: 10px;">
          <p>• The 2013 General Instructions for Form W-2G and 5754.</p>
          <p>To order these instructions and additional forms, go to www.irs.gov/w2g or call 1-800-TAX-FORM.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div style="width: 50%;">
        <div style="font-weight: bold;">Copy A. For State, City, or Local Tax Department</div>
        <div style="margin-top: 10px;">
          <p>Report this income on your state, city, or local income tax return. If required.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
          <div style="font-weight: bold;">Copy B. For Winner's Records</div>
          <div style="margin-top: 10px;">
            <p>This is important tax information and is being furnished to the Internal Revenue Service. If you are required to file a return, you must use this form to report this income tax withheld in this copy to attach this copy to your return.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
          <div style="font-weight: bold;">Copy C. For Payer</div>
          <div style="margin-top: 10px;">
            <p>This copy is for the payer's records.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div style="margin-top: 30px; font-size: 9pt;">
    <p>Foreign winners. Use Form 1042-S, Foreign Person's U.S. Source Income Subject to Withholding, to report gambling winnings paid to nonresident aliens and foreign corporations. See the Instructions for Form 1042-S.</p>
    <p>For more information, see Pub. 529, Taxable and Nontaxable Income.</p>
  </div>
</div>